# Columns of the selfie's picture.
#
# The picture is cut into tiles 32 columns wide, and a column is △ h (△ u o):
# o columns into tile h, with u = 31 − o columns left to the tile's end.
# Keeping both makes a step either way cheap: going right takes one from u and
# adds one to o, and where u is 0 the next tile starts (cinc); going left is
# the same the other way round (cdec). x0 is the first column of tile 0.

# 25, the window's size; 32, a tile's (b1); and 64 (b2).
n25 = \iter iter 0 25 Snat.succ
b1 = \iter iter 0 32 Snat.succ
b2 = \b1 \church church b1 Snat.succ _ b1
cinc = \n31 \inc Pair.match $ \h Pair.match $ \u \o △ (△ (\h Pair.create (inc h) (Pair.create n31 0)) (\u \h Pair.create h (Pair.create u (Snat.succ o)))) _ u h
cdec = \n31 \dec Pair.match $ \h Pair.match $ \u △ (△ (Pair.create (dec h) (Pair.create 0 n31)) (\o Pair.create h (Pair.create (Snat.succ u) o))) _
x0 = \n31 Pair.create 0 (Pair.create n31 0)
# [nz c]: c with its u and o rebuilt as parts of the one 31 that everything
# is passed, so that the columns kept for the whole show share their numbers
# instead of each holding its own.
nz = \n31 \dec \church Pair.match $ \h Pair.match $ \u \o Pair.create h (Pair.create (church o dec _ n31) (church u dec _ n31))
# [le a b x y]: x if column a is not right of column b, else y.
le = \inc \dec \church (\diff \a \b \x \y Pair.match (\ha \uoa Pair.match (\hb
    △ (△ (\uob △ (△ x (\_ y)) (\_ \_ x) (diff (Pair.snd uob) (Pair.snd uoa))) (\_ \_ y)) (\_ \_ \_ x)
      (diff hb ha))
  b) a) (\m \n church m dec inc n)
